# Build context for docker/Dockerfile is the REPO ROOT, because the single
# image needs both the backend and frontend trees. That makes this file the
# one that matters - backend/.dockerignore and frontend/.dockerignore are only
# consulted when their own folder is the context, which is no longer the case.
#
# Two things this has to get right:
#
#   1. node_modules. The ui stage does `npm install` and then `COPY frontend/ .`,
#      so without the line below a Windows host's node_modules would be copied
#      over the container's freshly installed Linux one - native binaries and
#      all - and the build would use the wrong platform's packages.
#
#   2. env files. A real .env.prod on the build machine must never end
#      up in an image layer. Production config reaches the container at RUN
#      time through the .env.prod volume mount (see docker-compose.prod.yaml),
#      never at build time. VITE_* values are passed with --build-arg instead;
#      a stray .env in the context could otherwise be picked up by Vite and
#      silently override them.

# --- frontend ---
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# --- backend ---
backend/__pycache__
backend/**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
backend/.venv
backend/venv
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache

# --- config: nothing from here is ever baked in ---
config/

# Belt and braces, in case an env file is left somewhere else.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- not needed by the build ---
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
release/
images/
docs/
deploy/
scripts/
README.md
docker-compose*.yaml
docker-compose*.yml
